# Re-arm CEC whenever the HDMI link comes back.
#
# The connector is held in DRM_FORCE_ON_DIGITAL so the sink survives the
# receiver being switched off, which also means DRM never runs a real detect
# and the CEC adapter never gets a physical address. cec-rearm.sh borrows one
# detect to fetch it; this rule runs that again each time the receiver is
# switched on, since a power cycle can drop the address.
#
# The script is idempotent and takes a lock, so the extra change events its own
# status writes generate settle out after one no-op run.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", ENV{HOTPLUG}=="1", \
    TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="cec-rearm.service"
